From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SwitchVN <switchvn@example.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qasf/dmowrapper: decommit output allocators before taking the
 streaming lock

Skipping video playback could hang the whole application:

  err:sync:RtlpWaitForCriticalSection section 16FA21CC
    "libs/strmbase/filter.c: strmbase_filter.stream_cs"
    wait timed out in thread 0144, blocked by 0368, retrying (60 sec)

Thread 0368 is the streaming thread of the DMO wrapper hosting the WMA
decoder.  It is inside process_output(), blocked in IMemAllocator_GetBuffer()
because the renderer downstream still holds every buffer.  strmbase calls
Receive() with the filter's streaming lock held, so 0368 sits on that lock
for as long as GetBuffer() blocks.

Thread 0144 stops the graph.  It stops the renderer, reaches the decoder and
calls dmo_wrapper_cleanup_stream(), which took the streaming lock before
decommitting the output allocators -- but decommitting is exactly what makes
the blocked GetBuffer() fail and let 0368 release the lock.  Neither thread
can proceed.

dmo_wrapper_begin_flush() already forwards downstream without holding the
lock for the same reason.  Do the same here and decommit first.

Found on ATRI -My Dear Moments- (AppId 1230140), which hangs when its
opening video is skipped.
---
 dlls/qasf/dmowrapper.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/qasf/dmowrapper.c b/dlls/qasf/dmowrapper.c
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/dlls/qasf/dmowrapper.c
+++ b/dlls/qasf/dmowrapper.c
@@ -950,13 +950,19 @@
 
     IUnknown_QueryInterface(filter->dmo, &IID_IMediaObject, (void **)&dmo);
 
-    EnterCriticalSection(&filter->filter.stream_cs);
+    /* Decommit the output allocators before taking the streaming lock.
+     * process_output() blocks in IMemAllocator_GetBuffer() when downstream
+     * holds every buffer, and it does so from Receive(), which strmbase calls
+     * with the streaming lock held.  Decommitting is what makes that call
+     * fail and release the lock, so it has to happen first or the two sides
+     * wait for each other forever. */
     for (i = 0; i < filter->source_count; ++i)
     {
         if (filter->sources[i].pin.pin.peer)
             IMemAllocator_Decommit(filter->sources[i].pin.pAllocator);
     }
 
+    EnterCriticalSection(&filter->filter.stream_cs);
     IMediaObject_Flush(dmo);
     IMediaObject_FreeStreamingResources(dmo);
 
